"comparison": "Both AVGO and AMD disclose specific programs aimed at employee skills development and career advancement. AVGO's 'Beyond Code Programs' focus on skills development and upskilling within the context of mainframe technology to help customers, while AMD offers specialized manager/leadership development programs and tuition reimbursement to help its own employees advance their careers. While AVGO's initiative is framed as a customer value-add service, AMD's is an internal human capital investment; however, both explicitly address 'skills development' and 'training' as key mechanisms for workforce capability. AVGO states its programs address 'skills development, staffing... and educating and upskilling the workforce' (avgo_2024_1_P025_S012), whereas AMD states it 'provide[s] specialized development programs for our employees as well as educational assistance in the form of tuition reimbursement' (amd_2024_1_P085_S003).",
